WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.434
Just outside Ciudad Juarez.

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.236
And this is the last train

00:00:03.236 --> 00:00:04.971
stop for this freight train

00:00:04.971 --> 00:00:05.505
that's eventually

00:00:05.505 --> 00:00:06.606
going to head into the city.

00:00:06.606 --> 00:00:08.008
And you can see already

00:00:08.008 --> 00:00:09.642
dozens of migrants

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:12.746
in several of these cars on top of them

00:00:13.046 --> 00:00:14.147
all about.

00:00:14.147 --> 00:00:16.249
They're asking us if we have water,

00:00:16.416 --> 00:00:17.684
we have food.

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:21.621
We climb on

00:00:22.789 --> 00:00:24.791
the train slowly starts up again,

00:00:24.791 --> 00:00:25.692
heading north.

00:00:25.692 --> 00:00:28.728
We meet migrants from all over Honduras.

00:00:28.795 --> 00:00:30.597
And this is from Honduras

00:00:30.597 --> 00:00:33.133
originally and wants to go to the US.

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:35.301
Felipe and Marcela from Colombia,

00:00:35.502 --> 00:00:39.339
also hoping to enter the U.S.

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:41.975
I asked her why the U.S.

00:00:41.975 --> 00:00:44.077
she said to have a better future.

00:00:45.545 --> 00:00:47.881
Omar from Venezuela

00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:49.149
in Baltimore,

00:00:49.149 --> 00:00:51.151
is trying to get to Baltimore, Maryland.

00:00:51.151 --> 00:00:52.952
We rode for an hour.

00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:54.587
They've been on here for days.

00:00:54.587 --> 00:00:56.990
12 days for Roberto and his family.

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:59.025
I'm here, man.

00:00:59.025 --> 00:01:00.894
He's with his dad and his sister.

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:05.765
I had no role.

00:01:05.765 --> 00:01:07.100
You know, he's all done.

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:07.867
She has.

00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:10.637
And the door says they've been attacked.

00:01:10.637 --> 00:01:12.305
They've been robbed.

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:15.642
Describes a really treacherous track.

00:01:16.443 --> 00:01:18.144
Part of the train journey north for some

00:01:18.144 --> 00:01:20.313
is on what's called La Bestia The Beast.

00:01:20.547 --> 00:01:21.181
It's also known

00:01:21.181 --> 00:01:22.715
as the train of death

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:25.952
and often controlled by cartels.

00:01:25.952 --> 00:01:27.554
Roberto wears a facemask

00:01:27.554 --> 00:01:29.289
to not infect the others, tells me

00:01:29.289 --> 00:01:33.093
he got sick early on in his travels

00:01:33.093 --> 00:01:34.260
There's a lot of them have been sick.

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:35.462
And over the journey,

00:01:35.462 --> 00:01:37.530
they believe these two kids, young ones.

00:01:38.231 --> 00:01:40.633
He tells me his two toddlers nearly died.

00:01:40.733 --> 00:01:41.534
So we sent them back

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:42.769
with family in Honduras

00:01:42.769 --> 00:01:44.771
as he continues on.

00:01:44.771 --> 00:01:47.040
They stand, sit and sleep

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:48.875
on metal construction beams

00:01:48.875 --> 00:01:51.077
covered in plastic, dirty clothes.

00:01:51.077 --> 00:01:52.011
And cardboard

00:01:52.011 --> 00:01:53.613
used to make it as comfortable

00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:54.714
as possible.

00:01:54.714 --> 00:01:57.183
The heat and sun brutal at night.

00:01:57.383 --> 00:01:58.551
It's the cold and wind.

00:01:59.619 --> 00:02:01.754
The smells arrange

00:02:01.754 --> 00:02:04.958
sewage at times and burning trash

00:02:05.158 --> 00:02:06.059
as we drove past

00:02:06.059 --> 00:02:08.394
what appears to be an incinerator.

00:02:08.394 --> 00:02:11.364
Their souls worn down on

00:02:13.166 --> 00:02:16.469
and through your body.

00:02:16.469 --> 00:02:17.637
Is

00:02:19.205 --> 00:02:21.207
just legal.

00:02:21.207 --> 00:02:23.343
It's very dangerous for women, too.

00:02:23.343 --> 00:02:24.177
And they said food

00:02:24.177 --> 00:02:26.246
is is just really scarce right now.

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:28.014
If you call me that dog.

00:02:28.014 --> 00:02:28.515
Not anymore.

00:02:28.515 --> 00:02:29.415
I wish to see him again.

00:02:29.415 --> 00:02:32.085
Forget the walking down the aisle.

00:02:32.085 --> 00:02:34.287
Omar spent four days on board already.

00:02:34.721 --> 00:02:36.689
Food is run out.

00:02:36.689 --> 00:02:37.824
He showed us the little water

00:02:37.824 --> 00:02:38.791
he has left.

00:02:38.791 --> 00:02:39.492
And the documents.

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:42.061
He clings to keeping secured in plastic

00:02:42.562 --> 00:02:43.329
the gates.

00:02:43.596 --> 00:02:44.964
But the main thing is,

00:02:44.964 --> 00:02:45.798
I don't know where they're

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:47.066
going to settle for

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:50.403
so long as he's ready

00:02:50.403 --> 00:02:52.539
for all the different situations

00:02:52.539 --> 00:02:54.107
that would allow you to enter the U.S..

00:02:54.107 --> 00:02:56.209
And he's got it printed out in Spanish,

00:02:58.611 --> 00:03:01.080
and he's got it the address.

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:02.048
And so I'm able

00:03:02.048 --> 00:03:04.751
to have his friend in Baltimore

00:03:05.051 --> 00:03:07.120
that he hopes to get to us

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:10.924
said, and that gives you money

00:03:11.324 --> 00:03:12.959
for days on the train for him.

00:03:12.959 --> 00:03:14.260
He said the first day

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:15.428
you just got really sick

00:03:15.428 --> 00:03:18.531
because the sun was just so strong

00:03:18.531 --> 00:03:20.567
and now he's making sure to keep covered

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:22.202
as much as possible.

00:03:22.202 --> 00:03:24.604
He wants to go to New York for Omar.

00:03:24.604 --> 00:03:25.838
It's a familiar journey.

00:03:25.838 --> 00:03:27.941
He left Venezuela six months ago,

00:03:27.941 --> 00:03:30.043
already expelled once from the U.S.

00:03:30.043 --> 00:03:31.477
for trying to cross.

00:03:31.477 --> 00:03:33.947
He'll try again when you get a legal

00:03:36.482 --> 00:03:38.218
whether legally

00:03:38.218 --> 00:03:41.754
or illegally, he will cross, he tells me.

00:03:42.322 --> 00:03:45.425
I ask him if he's hopeful

00:03:45.425 --> 00:03:47.760
that that is easy for him, which I fear.

00:03:48.061 --> 00:03:50.163
I've got a lot of faith, he tells me.

00:03:50.863 --> 00:03:51.931
Ultimately,

00:03:51.931 --> 00:03:53.666
he hopes to get the money

00:03:53.666 --> 00:03:55.668
sent back to his kids in Venezuela.

00:03:56.135 --> 00:03:57.003
Which is a good idea

00:03:58.037 --> 00:03:58.671
because

00:04:01.074 --> 00:04:01.774
as we pull in this

00:04:01.774 --> 00:04:03.643
year that Juarez, about 25 miles

00:04:03.643 --> 00:04:04.444
still from the border

00:04:04.444 --> 00:04:05.845
wall with El Paso,

00:04:05.845 --> 00:04:08.348
we and the others climb out

00:04:08.348 --> 00:04:08.781
and that's it.

00:04:08.781 --> 00:04:09.983
You can see

00:04:10.183 --> 00:04:11.351
almost everyone now getting off.

00:04:11.351 --> 00:04:13.453
It's basically the last stop.

00:04:13.453 --> 00:04:15.488
Omar among the last off

00:04:15.488 --> 00:04:18.324
carrying his only belongings and somehow

00:04:18.858 --> 00:04:20.226
a smile.

00:04:20.693 --> 00:04:21.494
I mean, at

00:04:22.262 --> 00:04:22.829
some point

00:04:22.829 --> 00:04:25.465
is planning to cross immediately

00:04:26.199 --> 00:04:28.968
He ran across highway, not around.

00:04:29.369 --> 00:04:32.238
Then he went up

00:04:34.741 --> 00:04:35.842
and we're giving you a live

00:04:35.842 --> 00:04:36.643
look right now

00:04:36.643 --> 00:04:37.710
at the destination

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:39.712
for those migrants who are on board

00:04:39.712 --> 00:04:41.514
that train along with us.

00:04:41.514 --> 00:04:43.049
And you can see some changes

00:04:43.049 --> 00:04:45.385
that we've noticed in the past hour

00:04:45.385 --> 00:04:45.985
or so, Jake.

00:04:45.985 --> 00:04:46.986
We've shown you this spot

00:04:46.986 --> 00:04:47.854
over the past couple of days,

00:04:47.854 --> 00:04:49.822
but there's two large groups now.

00:04:49.822 --> 00:04:51.691
And it seems that Texas National Guard

00:04:51.691 --> 00:04:54.460
along potentially with CBP are separating

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:56.462
single men to the far side

00:04:56.462 --> 00:04:58.131
and then closer to where we are.

00:04:58.131 --> 00:04:59.432
Mostly families are together.

00:04:59.432 --> 00:05:00.233
And some of these families

00:05:00.233 --> 00:05:00.967
we're starting to see

00:05:00.967 --> 00:05:02.235
take their belongings

00:05:02.235 --> 00:05:03.603
and toss them into

00:05:03.603 --> 00:05:05.071
a big essentially dumpster.

00:05:05.071 --> 00:05:05.772
And that's

00:05:05.772 --> 00:05:07.040
usually typical of what happens

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:08.241
before they're going to be processed

00:05:08.241 --> 00:05:09.709
and allowed into the U.S.

00:05:09.709 --> 00:05:11.711
to go forward with their claims of asylum

00:05:12.078 --> 00:05:12.912
with the single men

00:05:12.912 --> 00:05:14.280
who have been taken aside

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:15.882
and put into another group.

00:05:15.882 --> 00:05:16.549
It's very likely

00:05:16.549 --> 00:05:17.450
that if

00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:19.085
it's following any sort of precedents

00:05:19.085 --> 00:05:20.586
that we've seen in the past,

00:05:20.586 --> 00:05:22.088
they'll be brought back over the border

00:05:22.088 --> 00:05:24.324
from the U.S. right here to Mexico.

00:05:24.657 --> 00:05:26.592
And that's part of the deportation

00:05:26.592 --> 00:05:27.260
expulsions

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:28.661
that we've seen under Title 42.

00:05:28.661 --> 00:05:29.462
So it's very possible

00:05:29.462 --> 00:05:30.663
that's exactly what's happened to that

00:05:30.663 --> 00:05:31.531
group, Jake.

00:05:31.531 --> 00:05:31.798
All right.

00:05:31.798 --> 00:05:32.398
David Culver

00:05:32.398 --> 00:05:33.333
with some important reporting.

00:05:33.333 --> 00:05:34.300
Thank you so much.

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:34.634
Joining me

00:05:34.634 --> 00:05:35.368
now to discuss

00:05:35.368 --> 00:05:36.869
is blasting as yet, though.

00:05:36.869 --> 00:05:38.571
He is the assistant secretary for border

00:05:38.571 --> 00:05:39.472
and immigration policy

00:05:39.472 --> 00:05:41.708
at the Department of Homeland. Security.

00:05:41.708 --> 00:05:43.876
Thank you so much for joining us today

00:05:43.876 --> 00:05:46.112
on such a busy day.

00:05:46.112 --> 00:05:46.846
What are you?

00:05:46.846 --> 00:05:48.047
What are your intelligence sources

00:05:48.047 --> 00:05:48.981
telling you

00:05:48.981 --> 00:05:51.317
about how many migrants the U.S.

00:05:51.317 --> 00:05:53.186
could be encountering daily?

00:05:53.186 --> 00:05:54.153
Well, we've already heard it's

00:05:54.153 --> 00:05:56.122
been over 10,000 a day.

00:05:56.122 --> 00:05:57.990
Are you expecting after midnight tonight?

00:05:57.990 --> 00:05:59.926
15,000. 20,000 a day?

00:05:59.926 --> 00:06:00.793
What are you expecting

00:06:03.229 --> 00:06:03.496
Yeah.

00:06:03.496 --> 00:06:04.163
Thank you very much,

00:06:04.163 --> 00:06:06.566
Jake, for having me on the show today.

00:06:07.233 --> 00:06:08.067
Look, we know that

00:06:08.067 --> 00:06:10.837
there are many thousands of migrants

00:06:11.237 --> 00:06:13.439
you know, in Mexico and along the transit

00:06:13.439 --> 00:06:15.475
routes coming north,

00:06:15.475 --> 00:06:18.311
you know, seeking to access our border.

00:06:18.344 --> 00:06:20.246
We have been working

00:06:20.246 --> 00:06:22.615
closely with our regional partners,

00:06:22.615 --> 00:06:24.050
including the government of Mexico,

00:06:24.050 --> 00:06:24.417
in order

00:06:24.417 --> 00:06:26.552
to, you know, increase enforcement

00:06:26.552 --> 00:06:28.354
on those routes.

00:06:28.354 --> 00:06:28.621
You know,

00:06:28.621 --> 00:06:29.722
we have been averaging

00:06:29.722 --> 00:06:32.091
about 10,000 encounters a day.

00:06:32.792 --> 00:06:33.860
The last few days,

00:06:33.860 --> 00:06:35.128
you know, this is, you know,

00:06:35.128 --> 00:06:36.162
what we've been planning for,

00:06:36.162 --> 00:06:37.196
frankly, for the better

00:06:37.196 --> 00:06:39.365
part of two years.

00:06:39.365 --> 00:06:40.333
We always knew that

00:06:40.333 --> 00:06:40.967
the days

00:06:40.967 --> 00:06:42.735
leading up to the lifting of Title 42

00:06:42.735 --> 00:06:43.269
and immediately

00:06:43.269 --> 00:06:44.937
after it were going to be challenging.

00:06:44.937 --> 00:06:45.705
And that's

00:06:45.772 --> 00:06:46.806
why we have been,

00:06:46.806 --> 00:06:47.740
you know, relentlessly

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:49.942
focused on preparing for it for so long.

00:06:49.942 --> 00:06:51.444
You just said and Secretary,

00:06:51.444 --> 00:06:52.612
my caucus has previously said

00:06:52.612 --> 00:06:53.479
you've been preparing for this

00:06:53.479 --> 00:06:54.180
for nearly two years.

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:54.814
If that's the case,

00:06:54.814 --> 00:06:57.016
why are you only just now

00:06:57.016 --> 00:06:58.885
surging these people, U.S.

00:06:58.885 --> 00:07:00.853
officials, to help out at the border?

00:07:00.853 --> 00:07:03.189
And why hasn't there been a bigger effort

00:07:03.189 --> 00:07:04.257
over the last two years

00:07:04.257 --> 00:07:06.459
knowing that this day would come

00:07:06.459 --> 00:07:09.128
to better convey and better prevent

00:07:09.695 --> 00:07:11.197
all of these undocumented

00:07:11.197 --> 00:07:12.799
individuals from coming into the country

00:07:15.601 --> 00:07:16.235
So we

00:07:16.235 --> 00:07:16.702
have, in

00:07:16.702 --> 00:07:17.537
point of fact,

00:07:17.537 --> 00:07:18.037
you know, been

00:07:18.037 --> 00:07:19.772
deploying people to the border

00:07:19.772 --> 00:07:21.407
on temporary details,

00:07:21.407 --> 00:07:23.176
you know, hundreds of them at a time

00:07:23.176 --> 00:07:25.077
now for the better part of two years.

00:07:25.077 --> 00:07:26.078
We have,

00:07:26.145 --> 00:07:27.313
over the last two years

00:07:27.313 --> 00:07:28.981
been adding holding capacity

00:07:28.981 --> 00:07:29.849
at the border.

00:07:29.849 --> 00:07:31.984
You know, CBP facilities can hold 7000

00:07:31.984 --> 00:07:33.920
more people today than they could

00:07:33.920 --> 00:07:34.687
two years ago.

00:07:34.687 --> 00:07:36.355
So we have been preparing

00:07:36.355 --> 00:07:37.256
I would point out

00:07:37.256 --> 00:07:38.524
that, you know, we asked Congress

00:07:38.524 --> 00:07:40.059
for $4.9 billion

00:07:40.059 --> 00:07:40.660
to help prepare

00:07:40.660 --> 00:07:42.361
for the lifting of Title 42.

00:07:42.361 --> 00:07:43.729
We got less than half of that

00:07:43.729 --> 00:07:44.497
from the Congress.

00:07:44.497 --> 00:07:45.932
So we are working,

00:07:45.932 --> 00:07:47.166
you know, within the resources

00:07:47.166 --> 00:07:47.900
we've been given

00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:49.502
and the statutes we have, which are,

00:07:49.502 --> 00:07:50.870
frankly, you know, broken

00:07:50.870 --> 00:07:53.506
and haven't been updated in decades.

00:07:53.506 --> 00:07:55.975
To deal with this challenge that we,

00:07:56.142 --> 00:07:57.410
you know, knew was coming

00:07:58.377 --> 00:07:58.778
during.

00:07:58.778 --> 00:08:00.046
It was almost

00:08:00.046 --> 00:08:01.414
2 million undocumented

00:08:01.414 --> 00:08:03.082
immigrants were thought to have it

00:08:03.082 --> 00:08:05.017
come to us

00:08:05.017 --> 00:08:07.620
during the first year of President Obama,

00:08:07.620 --> 00:08:09.489
the first 12 months, October to October.

00:08:09.489 --> 00:08:10.656
Most of that president

00:08:10.656 --> 00:08:12.825
I'm sorry, President Biden

00:08:13.025 --> 00:08:13.392
what do you think

00:08:13.392 --> 00:08:15.361
the number is going to be in a year?

00:08:15.361 --> 00:08:16.963
I mean, do you think this is going to be

00:08:16.963 --> 00:08:18.331
the biggest surge

00:08:18.331 --> 00:08:19.665
of undocumented immigrants

00:08:19.665 --> 00:08:21.033
and migrants coming into the U.S.

00:08:21.033 --> 00:08:21.767
ever

00:08:24.904 --> 00:08:25.171
Yeah.

00:08:25.171 --> 00:08:26.038
So there's little doubt

00:08:26.038 --> 00:08:26.939
that the last few years

00:08:26.939 --> 00:08:28.274
we've seen, you know,

00:08:28.274 --> 00:08:29.942
a surge in migration,

00:08:29.942 --> 00:08:32.011
that that has been large

00:08:32.011 --> 00:08:34.146
and we have, you know, reached numbers

00:08:34.146 --> 00:08:36.349
that we have not previously seen.

00:08:36.349 --> 00:08:36.749
That said,

00:08:36.749 --> 00:08:38.918
we've also over the last two years,

00:08:38.918 --> 00:08:39.719
you know, expelled

00:08:39.719 --> 00:08:40.553
more than 3 million

00:08:40.553 --> 00:08:42.255
people from the United States,

00:08:42.255 --> 00:08:44.524
which is also a record.

00:08:44.524 --> 00:08:45.424
So, you know, as

00:08:45.424 --> 00:08:47.760
we think about the lifting of Title 42,

00:08:48.094 --> 00:08:48.394
you know,

00:08:48.394 --> 00:08:50.897
we will return to immigration processes,

00:08:50.897 --> 00:08:52.465
which as one of your correspondents

00:08:52.465 --> 00:08:54.200
noted, takes take longer.

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:56.369
However, they also carry with them

00:08:56.369 --> 00:08:58.271
significant consequences for people

00:08:58.271 --> 00:08:59.105
who are removed,

00:08:59.105 --> 00:09:01.407
consequences that don't exist

00:09:01.407 --> 00:09:01.874
for people

00:09:01.874 --> 00:09:03.743
who are expelled under Title 42.

00:09:03.743 --> 00:09:06.212
And so we believe that the measures

00:09:06.212 --> 00:09:06.879
that we have taken,

00:09:06.879 --> 00:09:08.347
including the rule

00:09:08.347 --> 00:09:09.815
that was published today,

00:09:09.815 --> 00:09:11.484
which put some conditions

00:09:11.484 --> 00:09:13.252
on asylum eligibility for people

00:09:13.252 --> 00:09:15.354
who don't use lawful pathways, will,

00:09:15.955 --> 00:09:17.323
over time,

00:09:17.323 --> 00:09:18.591
you know, reduce the numbers

00:09:18.591 --> 00:09:20.026
we're seeing at the border.

00:09:20.026 --> 00:09:21.294
Does the United States have enough

00:09:23.262 --> 00:09:24.363
means

00:09:24.363 --> 00:09:28.868
to take care of the potentially millions

00:09:29.402 --> 00:09:30.069
of people

00:09:30.069 --> 00:09:32.672
who will be in a humanitarian crisis

00:09:33.339 --> 00:09:35.575
at the border in Chicago,

00:09:35.575 --> 00:09:38.311
in New York and Miami? I mean,

00:09:38.311 --> 00:09:40.379
are we going to be able to

00:09:40.379 --> 00:09:42.982
to to help these people?

00:09:42.982 --> 00:09:44.250
It just seems like

00:09:44.250 --> 00:09:47.420
we're already stretched so thin

00:09:49.322 --> 00:09:51.090
And that's a great question, Jake.

00:09:51.090 --> 00:09:52.224
I would say that, you know,

00:09:52.224 --> 00:09:53.025
we have been working

00:09:53.025 --> 00:09:54.093
closely with cities

00:09:54.093 --> 00:09:55.328
throughout the country

00:09:55.328 --> 00:09:57.563
and with NGOs to build capacity

00:09:57.630 --> 00:09:59.131
to receive migrants

00:09:59.131 --> 00:10:01.000
and to transport them.

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:01.968
But these are the costs

00:10:01.968 --> 00:10:03.936
of our fundamentally broken

00:10:03.936 --> 00:10:05.871
immigration and asylum system.

00:10:05.871 --> 00:10:06.072
You know,

00:10:06.072 --> 00:10:07.473
the president has asked

00:10:07.473 --> 00:10:08.474
Congress on day

00:10:08.474 --> 00:10:10.142
one of this administration

00:10:10.142 --> 00:10:11.210
to come together

00:10:11.210 --> 00:10:11.611
on work

00:10:11.611 --> 00:10:12.945
on a bipartisan basis

00:10:12.945 --> 00:10:15.114
on immigration reform.

00:10:15.414 --> 00:10:17.283
We have not seen that from Congress.

00:10:17.283 --> 00:10:18.918
And as one of your correspondents

00:10:18.918 --> 00:10:20.219
noted, you've seen

00:10:20.219 --> 00:10:22.121
now these surges in migration happen

00:10:22.121 --> 00:10:22.989
under presidents

00:10:22.989 --> 00:10:26.125
of both political parties who have tried

00:10:26.125 --> 00:10:26.792
to deal with this

00:10:26.792 --> 00:10:29.161
through executive action, as we have.

00:10:29.161 --> 00:10:30.329
But until we get, you

00:10:30.329 --> 00:10:31.831
know, Congress to come together

00:10:31.831 --> 00:10:33.833
and meaningfully reform our laws,

00:10:33.833 --> 00:10:34.066
you know,

00:10:34.066 --> 00:10:34.667
I think we're going to

00:10:34.667 --> 00:10:35.935
continue to see these surges.

